# Frontmatter exemptions — read by tenet-audit/scripts/frontmatter-check.sh
# One shell glob per line, relative to the repo root. '*' crosses directories.
# Everything not listed here must carry title/type/status/updated.

# A vault is not a code repository, and it runs a different frontmatter schema on
# purpose: type/created/status/scope, plus revisit and the link properties. That
# schema is what promote.sh and resolve.sh read, and it is documented in the tenet
# skill's references/conventions.md.
#
# Without these lines the auditor reports every note in the vault as a defect,
# which is the false-alarm rate that teaches a reader to skip the digest. The
# first glob alone covers the whole vault; the rest are here to say which genre
# each directory holds, so a future reader knows what was deliberate.

# Knowledge notes in the root: type/created/status/scope, no title (the filename
# is the title) and no updated (git carries that).
*.md

# Drafts awaiting review, same schema.
inbox/*

# The vault's own bookkeeping: type + title, no status or updated. These are
# living files rewritten in place, so an `updated` field would be stale between
# every edit and the next sweep.
_meta/*

# Note templates. They carry the schema they are templates for, including the
# Obsidian {{date}} placeholders, which are not valid values yet.
templates/*

# Raw source material, kept as received. Its companion `source` note carries the
# metadata; copying it here would be the duplication raw/ exists to avoid.
raw/*
